  "method": "One-off pywin32 COM script, Excel visible (needed for ActiveWindow). For each font x size: new workbook, wb.Styles('Normal').Font.Name/.Size set, then Columns B..E .ColumnWidth = 8.43/10/30/100. Recorded Columns(x).Width (points) and .ColumnWidth for A (default) and B..E, sheet StandardWidth, and ActiveWindow PointsToScreenPixelsX(0)/(72)/(720) with Zoom (pixels per 72pt ~ screen DPI). Saved .xlsx only.",
  "dpi": {
    "probe_process_not_dpi_aware": {
      "GetDpiForSystem": 96,
      "LOGPIXELSX": 96
    },
    "per_monitor_dpi_aware": {
      "GetDpiForSystem": 96,
      "LOGPIXELSX": 96,
      "screen_px": [
        3200,
        2000
      ]
    },
    "note": "The capture process (python.exe) was not DPI-aware, so its GetDpiForSystem/LOGPIXELSX and the PointsToScreenPixelsX readings may be DPI-virtualized; per_monitor_dpi_aware was queried afterwards from a separate process with SetProcessDpiAwareness(2)."
  },
